Physical Geology, second edition — Steven Earle (@geo-physical: 0, is #reference, #part-of @geo-sources) { r_5GWEYVQGR176TXMQT0S881ZSKX
Steven Earle, with contributing faculty and Karla Panchuk. Physical Geology, second edition. BCcampus, 2019. Ebook ISBN 978-1-77420-028-5. [Publisher’s complete book and authorized downloads](https://opentextbc.ca/physicalgeology2ed/) · [Component exceptions](https://opentextbc.ca/physicalgeology2ed/front-matter/exceptions-to-the-cc-by-licence/).

Read the complete 22-chapter textbook with exercises. It develops minerals/rocks, time, Earth's interior, tectonics, earthquakes, structures, surface/water systems, climate, resources, western Canada's history, and planetary origins. Western Canadian examples are a sustained regional case, not a universal local map; compare them with the Brazilian study and other regions later.

The publisher states CC BY 4.0 except where otherwise noted and supplies specific component exceptions. Preserve author, edition, publisher, source, and actual notices when retaining or adapting. This trail links the book and authors original explanations; no text/media/PDF collection is bundled. Bibliography, chapter structure, access, licence, and exceptions checked on 29 October 2026.

